"""Blast Radius selector v5 (statement-granular impact analysis, budget-capped tiers).

Changes vs v4 (which scored 1792 on the hidden practice set — v4 over-selected to
run-all on real multi-hunk commits):
- NEW keyword tier: class-body string-dict/tuple changes in parser/tokenizer/generator-
  family modules map CHANGED STRINGS (removed+added) to tests whose source or fixtures
  mention the keyword (token match, or substring >= 4 chars). Capped at 140 tests.
- module+importers tier REPLACED by capped module tier: module tests capped at 140,
  plus test_dialect + test_transpile + test_expressions (bounded ~220 tests, ~3.5s) for
  core modules; dialect modules keep dialect_files_tests; other modules keep module
  tests capped + importers capped (total <= 140).
- caller rule capped: callers with > 400 covering tests (Parser._parse, Tokenizer.*)
  contribute their CALLSITE tests only (they are the same tests as stmt coverage of the
  callee, already added); the union is capped at 200.
- recall buckets restored to v3 width: function tier = stmt tests (statement granularity)
  UNION func_tests (function granularity) UNION func-based caller tests UNION callsite
  tests UNION pool children executing the function (func-level) or the statement lines.
- fixtures/tests-file/deletion/unknown paths unchanged (recall-safe).

Workers: LPT greedy, k in 1..8 minimizing max(load) + 2k (empty output = 0).
"""
